"short_summary":"A scheduled, ambassador-led introduction to Fresno State’s campus.","evidence_claim":"Fresno State Outreach and Special Programs says its campus tours are free of charge and offers both virtual and in-person reservations.","source_url":"https://studentaffairs.fresnostate.edu/outreach/services/","source_title":"Outreach Services - Recruitment","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The tour itself is free, but advance booking and weekday availability apply. Campus parking may require payment; use a no-cost arrival method to preserve the zero-dollar plan.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"cary-park-free-hang","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Cary Park","title":"Meet Up at Cary Park","subtitle":"Use a named Fresno neighborhood park for an outdoor group break.","notes":"Bring water and a blanket, choose an open shared area and keep the meetup informal so no facility reservation is needed.","short_summary":"An easy outdoor meetup in a city neighborhood park.","evidence_claim":"The City of Fresno identifies Cary Park as a neighborhood park, and its official parks fee table states that neighborhood parks have no entrance fee.","source_url":"https://www.fresno.gov/parks/parks-trails-facilities/","source_title":"Parks, Trails & Facilities","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"City neighborhood parks have no entrance fee. Use ordinary shared park space; reservations or organized facility use can carry separate requirements or charges.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"rotary-east-park-free-hang","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Rotary East Park","title":"Catch Up at Rotary East Park","subtitle":"Gather outdoors at a no-fee Fresno neighborhood park.","notes":"Pick a daylight meetup time, bring your own water and use an unreserved common area for conversation or a casual walk.","short_summary":"A purchase-free setting for a daylight conversation outdoors.","evidence_claim":"The City of Fresno lists Rotary East Park within its park system, whose official fee table assigns no entrance fee to neighborhood parks.","source_url":"https://www.fresno.gov/parks/parks-trails-facilities/","source_title":"Parks, Trails & Facilities","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"No neighborhood-park entrance fee is required. Avoid reservable facilities or paid organized uses if the outing must remain free.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"melody-park-free-hang","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Melody Park","title":"Take a Break at Melody Park","subtitle":"Meet on the grounds of a named city neighborhood park.","notes":"Bring a reusable water bottle, find an available common area and leave scheduled program spaces open for participants.","short_summary":"A simple neighborhood-park reset that requires no purchase.","evidence_claim":"The City of Fresno names Melody Park among its facilities, and the city’s parks fee table states that neighborhood parks charge no entrance fee.","source_url":"https://www.fresno.gov/parks/parks-trails-facilities/","source_title":"Parks, Trails & Facilities","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"General neighborhood-park entry has no fee. Separate classes, reservations or limited programs may have their own registration rules.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"todd-beamer-park-free-hang","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Todd Beamer Park","title":"Walk and Talk at Todd Beamer Park","subtitle":"Turn a city neighborhood park visit into a free social walk.","notes":"Set a visible meeting point, walk together through open public areas and bring sun protection during warm weather.","short_summary":"A no-purchase walk-and-talk destination in north Fresno.","evidence_claim":"Todd Beamer Park is identified by the City of Fresno, whose official parks page states that neighborhood parks have no entrance fee.","source_url":"https://www.fresno.gov/parks/parks-trails-facilities/","source_title":"Parks, Trails & Facilities","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"General entry to city neighborhood parks is free. Keep to open public areas and confirm any posted temporary restrictions upon arrival.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"orchid-park-free-hang","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Orchid Park","title":"Share a Picnic at Orchid Park","subtitle":"Bring food from home to a no-entrance-fee neighborhood park.","notes":"Use an open table or lawn without claiming exclusive space; bring everything from home and pack out the group’s waste.","short_summary":"A bring-your-own picnic option with no required transaction.","evidence_claim":"The City of Fresno identifies Orchid Park as a neighborhood park, and the city’s parks fee table says neighborhood parks have no entrance fee.","source_url":"https://www.fresno.gov/parks/parks-trails-facilities/","source_title":"Parks, Trails & Facilities","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Park entry is free, but exclusive use of the Orchid Picnic Pavilion requires a reservation. Use unreserved common space for a zero-dollar visit.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"tollhouse-park-free-hang","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Tollhouse Park","title":"Unplug at Tollhouse Park","subtitle":"Use a city neighborhood par