 a Group Reset at Einstein Park","subtitle":"Use a named Fresno neighborhood park for a free daytime meetup.","notes":"Agree on a short daylight window, meet in an open common area and bring any games, snacks or water from home.","short_summary":"A flexible, no-admission place for friends to decompress outdoors.","evidence_claim":"The City of Fresno identifies Einstein Park and its neighborhood center, while the official parks fee table specifies no entrance fee for neighborhood parks.","source_url":"https://www.fresno.gov/parks/parks-trails-facilities/","source_title":"Parks, Trails & Facilities","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Entrance to city neighborhood parks is free. Use ordinary public space rather than reservable facilities, and follow all posted hours and rules.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
